A||N||5||Alex4mula||Do I need to replace CompuCam, lifters, & rockrs in my rebuild?||||5||
Z||000000||Alex4mula||12-29-1999||10:44 AM||||At 88K miles I installed these Crane's components: CompuCam,lifters, push rods and roller tip rockers (1.5r). Now at 156K miles my engine needs a rebuild. Can/Should I reuse these components again? I know that I need to get at least new springs. I am planning a 3.1, 3.2 or 3.4 rebuild if possible. Thanks in advance.||||reg||5
Z||000001||batboy||12-29-1999||12:01 PM||||If you replace the cam, then you must replace the lifters too. Personally, I would buy new cam and lifters, especially if this is a high performance rebuild. Carefully inspect the rockers, if they are still in great condition, no reason you can't reuse them. If they have any wear, replace them. I like using new pushrods too. I prefer to spend some extra money and build my engines as good as possible, so it will be a long time before I have to pull it and rebuild it again.||||reg||1
Z||000002||HarryG||12-29-1999||01:41 PM||||If you haven't torn down the motor yet, make sure that you keep each lifter identified when you take them out. That way, if you reuse the cam, you can insure that each lifter ends up on the same cam lobe as it was originally run against.||||reg||1
Z||000003||terryk||12-29-1999||04:57 PM||||Withoug question, I would replace them. Period. Would you like to remove the engine again? <P>Timing chain too. The Cloyes True roller is a very good chain. Gives the engine more of a "machine" sound too.<P>Then some 1.6:1 rockers, and some ......<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||Alex4mula||12-30-1999||09:47 AM||||Thanks all for your help. After long research of options and info in this list I think I'll go the 3.2 way.||||reg||12
Z||000005||Eric||12-31-1999||12:10 AM||||I've heard things about those rocker arms.  I think it would be in your best interest to replace the rocker arms.  A lot of stress is put on the moving parts and you can't really tell how worn they are.  They are a performance option, so who knows how long they're meant to last. ||||reg||1
